<title>JAPAN: Tokyo precious metal futures closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo precious metal futures closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo precious metal futures market is closed on Wednesday for a national holiday. Trading will resume on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the benchmark December gold futures ended at 1,325 yen per gram. December platinum futures ended at 1,340 yen per gram, silver at 177.7 yen per 10 grams and palladium at 447 yen per gram.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
